---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Layout title="Pricing" description="Indicative Laissez pricing: free design partner pilots, a platform fee plus basis points for distributors, no charge for issuers, and exactly how an invoice is made." path="pricing/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Distributors pay for reach. Issuers integrate free.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Indicative pricing for 2027. The value shows up when a distributor sells a fund it could not sell before, so most of the price scales with value settled, not seats. The sandbox is free and needs no account.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta"><a class="btn primary" href={url('app/')}>Try the sandbox</a><a class="arrow-link" href={url('access/')}>Talk to us about a pilot</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap tiers">
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Design partner</h3>
        <p class="price">No platform fee<span>90-day pilot, test networks only</span></p>
        <p class="muted">For the first distributors and issuers taking one fund through one corridor. One slot is reserved for a reference customer: no platform fee in the first production year in exchange for a named case study and reference calls.</p>
        <ul class="ticks"><li>Sandbox and testnet access</li><li>Two jurisdictions, one fund, your corridor</li><li>Direct input into launch rule packs</li><li>Founder-led integration</li><li>Success measured on the public metrics: reuse, settlements, zero unchecked settlements, time to first settlement</li></ul>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={url('access/')}>Apply</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <span class="tag">Decide-only</span>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <p class="price">Flat annual fee<span>plus a price per allowed decision</span></p>
        <p class="muted">For banks that settle on their own rails and want Laissez for eligibility, evidence and monitoring. Settlement routes stay closed; what-if checks and refusals are free.</p>
        <ul class="ticks"><li>Every rule pack, every jurisdiction</li><li>Signed decision receipts and the audit log</li><li>Credential network and holder monitoring</li><li>Audit export to your SIEM or a write-once bucket</li></ul>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={`${url('app/')}#/settings/billing`}>Ask for a quote</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier feat">
        <span class="tag">For distributors</span>
        <h3>Platform</h3>
        <p class="price">From $60K a year<span>plus 1.5 bps of value settled</span></p>
        <p class="muted">For distributors selling tokenized funds across booking centers.</p>
        <ul class="ticks"><li>All rule packs, all jurisdictions</li><li>Credential network, investor portal, Travel Rule</li><li>Unlimited credentials and decisions</li><li>Atomic settlement in USDC, EURC and deposit tokens</li><li>Signed evidence receipts and exports</li></ul>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={url('access/')}>Request access</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Enterprise</h3>
        <p class="price">Custom</p>
        <p class="muted">For networks, fund administrators and banks running many corridors.</p>
        <ul class="ticks"><li>Private rule packs and policy templates</li><li>Dedicated environments</li><li>Volume pricing on settled value</li><li>Uptime and response commitments</li></ul>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={url('access/')}>Contact us</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <span class="tag">Data only</span>
        <h3>Rule packs</h3>
        <p class="price">Subscription<span>no settlement, no credentials</span></p>
        <p class="muted">The eligibility rules as a signed data feed for compliance teams: every jurisdiction's classes, the threshold test behind each with its citation and primary source, version history and a changelog. Included with every paid plan.</p>
        <ul class="ticks"><li>Signed, machine-readable feed your systems can pull</li><li>Versioned, dated, regression-tested</li><li>Change notices before a new version binds</li><li>Research only until counsel signs each pack</li></ul>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={url('developers/reference/')}>See the feed in the reference</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band light" id="roi">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>What it is worth to a distributor.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Three inputs from your own book. The outputs use the public figures cited on the home page: 143,617 registrations keep 14,769 funds sellable across borders, and distribution takes 48% of what EU fund investors pay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="roi" id="roi-calc">
        <div class="roi-in">
          <label>Cross-border AUM you distribute, USD<input id="roi-aum" type="number" min="0" step="1000000" value="2000000000" inputmode="numeric" /></label>
          <label>Booking centres<input id="roi-bc" type="number" min="1" max="50" value="3" inputmode="numeric" /></label>
          <label>Funds on the shelf<input id="roi-funds" type="number" min="1" max="2000" value="40" inputmode="numeric" /></label>
          <label>Cost of onboarding one client once, USD<input id="roi-kyc" type="number" min="0" step="100" value="2500" inputmode="numeric" /></label>
          <label>Clients onboarded a year<input id="roi-clients" type="number" min="0" step="10" value="400" inputmode="numeric" /></label>
        </div>
        <dl class="roi-out">
          <div><dt>Fund-by-centre registrations in play</dt><dd id="roi-regs">120</dd><p>funds times booking centres: the pairs that each need a legal position today</p></div>
          <div><dt>Repeat onboardings avoided a year</dt><dd id="roi-dup">$600,000</dd><p>clients re-papered at a second booking centre or a second fund, at your cost per onboarding, assuming 60% would otherwise be done twice</p></div>
          <div><dt>Laissez usage fee at 1.5 bps</dt><dd id="roi-fee">$300,000</dd><p>on the cross-border value settled in a year, plus the platform fee</p></div>
          <div><dt>Payback on the usage fee</dt><dd id="roi-pay">2.0x</dd><p>onboardings avoided divided by the usage fee. New shelf revenue is not counted.</p></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Change any input; the outputs recompute. The 60% repeat rate is an assumption you should replace with your own; the citations are on the <a class="text-link" href={url('sources/')}>sources page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };
      var ids = ['roi-aum', 'roi-bc', 'roi-funds', 'roi-kyc', 'roi-clients'];
      var money = function (n) { return '$' + Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US'); };
      var calc = function () {
        var aum = +$('roi-aum').value || 0, bc = +$('roi-bc').value || 1, funds = +$('roi-funds').value || 1, kyc = +$('roi-kyc').value || 0, clients = +$('roi-clients').value || 0;
        var regs = bc * funds;
        var dup = clients * 0.6 * kyc;
        var fee = aum * 0.00015;
        $('roi-regs').textContent = regs.toLocaleString('en-US');
        $('roi-dup').textContent = money(dup);
        $('roi-fee').textContent = money(fee);
        $('roi-pay').textContent = fee > 0 ? (dup / fee).toFixed(1) + 'x' : 'n/a';
      };
      ids.forEach(function (id) { $(id).addEventListener('input', calc); });
      calc();
    })();
  </script>
  <section class="band light">
    <div class="wrap cols-2">
      <div><h2>Price where the value lands.</h2></div>
      <div class="faq">
        <h4>Why are issuers free?</h4><p class="muted">The network is only useful if funds are on it. Charging issuers would slow the supply side that makes Laissez valuable to distributors.</p>
        <h4>Why basis points?</h4><p class="muted">A distributor’s gain is new cross-border volume it could not serve before. A small share of settled value aligns our revenue with that gain. At 1.5 bps, $1B settled costs $150K.</p>
        <h4>What does a decision cost?</h4><p class="muted">Nothing on its own. Pre-trade checks are free and unlimited so desks use them on every order, including the ones that never trade.</p>
        <h4>Do you take card or bank details?</h4><p class="muted">No. Where Stripe is connected, payment happens on Stripe's hosted invoice page by card or ACH. Otherwise you pay by bank transfer against the PDF and quote the invoice number, and we mark it paid when it arrives. Card and bank numbers never reach Laissez.</p>
        <h4>Can we take our data with us?</h4><p class="muted">Yes, at any time. An administrator can export every record in the organization, and the export keeps working after a billing suspension. Each person can also export or delete their own account data.</p>
        <h4>What if an invoice is late?</h4><p class="muted">One day after the due date the organization is marked past due and its administrators are emailed. At fourteen days they get a final warning. At thirty days the organization becomes read-only until the invoice is paid. Reads, exports, payment and redemptions keep working, because an investor's exit never depends on your invoice. Access restores itself when the invoice is paid.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" id="billing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>How a bill is made.</h2>
        <p class="lede">One order form, a platform fee each year, and a usage fee that follows what you settled. The Billing screen in the app shows this month's usage and the projected fee before anything becomes an invoice.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="bill">
        <li><h4>You accept an order form</h4><p>We send the plan, fees and payment terms as exact text. An administrator accepts it in the app. Laissez records their name, title, the time and a SHA-256 hash of the text they accepted.</p></li>
        <li><h4>The platform fee comes first</h4><p>Invoiced annually in advance on the start date and on each anniversary. Design partner pilots have none.</p></li>
        <li><h4>Usage follows settled value</h4><p>Basis points of the value of orders recorded as settled, counted per UTC day, invoiced monthly in arrears. Euro funds convert at the rate printed in the order form. Settlements later reverted are not counted.</p></li>
        <li><h4>You pay net 30</h4><p>Net 30 unless the order form says otherwise. Each invoice has a number, a PDF and the tax line your contract calls for.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <table class="ex">
        <caption>A distributor on the Platform plan, 1.5 bps, settling $40M in a month</caption>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Platform fee, annual, in advance</th><td>$60,000</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Usage fee for that month: $40,000,000 &times; 0.015%</th><td>$6,000</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Tax</th><td>Added only if the order form says so</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="hero-cta"><a class="btn primary" href={`${url('app/')}#/settings/billing`}>Ask for a quote in the sandbox</a><a class="arrow-link" href={url('terms/')}>Read the terms</a><a class="arrow-link" href={url('subprocessors/')}>See who processes data for us</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; align-items: stretch; }
  .tiers .tier:nth-child(4), .tiers .tier:nth-child(5) { grid-column: span 1; }
  .roi { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: start; }
  .roi-in { display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; }
  .roi-in label { display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .roi-in input { font: inherit; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); min-width: 0; }
  .roi-out { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 0; }
  .roi-out div { border-top: 2px solid var(--green); padding-top: 0.75rem; min-width: 0; }
  .roi-out dt { font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .roi-out dd { margin: 0.2rem 0 0.3rem; font-family: var(--f-display); font-size: 1.9rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink); }
  .roi-out p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .roi { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .roi-out { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .tier { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; }
  .tier.feat { border-color: var(--green); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .tag { align-self: flex-start; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--green); background: var(--green-wash); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem; }
  .price { font-family: var(--f-display); font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0.25rem 0 0; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .price span { display: block; font: 400 0.9rem var(--f-ui); color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: 0.35rem; }
  .tier .ticks { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .tier .arrow-link { margin-top: auto; }
  .faq h4 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .faq p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .bill { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); counter-reset: step; }
  .bill li { counter-increment: step; border-top: 2px solid var(--green); padding-top: 0.9rem; min-width: 0; }
  .bill li::before { content: counter(step); display: block; font: 500 0.82rem var(--f-mono); color: var(--green); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .bill h4 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .bill p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.94rem; }
  .ex { width: 100%; max-width: 40rem; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 0.96rem; }
  .ex caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); padding-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .ex th, .ex td { padding: 0.7rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; font-weight: 400; vertical-align: top; }
  .ex td { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink); padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .ex tbody tr:last-child th, .ex tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  #billing .hero-cta { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
